==================== BRIEF 04 lines 551-731 ====================
551: ## Investigation Brief 04
552: — Correction Notice Precedence
553: 
554: The corrections desk ships multiple notices per field. When several notices
555: target the same transaction and field, the notice with the lexicographically
556: greatest `effective` date wins. For each winning notice, `previous_value` in
557: `reconciliation_report.jsonl` is the field value immediately before that notice
558: applies (after ledger, amendments, and emails). Owner corrections override
559: both ledger owners and signed meeting amendments when applied in this step.
560: 
561: ## Investigation Brief 04
562: — Correction Notice Precedence — supporting chronology
563: 
564: Quality review #167 sampled 23 payroll accrual true-up tickets and found correction batch ordering whenever provisional ledger rows were not filtered before merge.
565: 
566: Lead reviewer A. Ndiaye opened working paper WP-8370 after HR finance reported that payroll accrual true-up distorted the May journal reconciliation. The team reconstructed mailbox ordering and found hold flag suppression affecting at least 5 transaction threads.
567: 
568: Draft sidebar (non-authoritative): some prototype tooling compared compliance mail timestamps against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. Brief 09 later in this archive supersedes that draft practice for production reconciliation.
569: 
570: Treasury liaison J. Huang explained that payroll accrual true-up related wires were paused during May journal, delaying compliance responses and amplifying status precedence inversion on rejected rows.
571: 
572: Stakeholder workshop #718 on payroll accrual true-up produced conflicting recollections about which correction notice superseded an earlier owner change; Brief 04 governs that precedence for automated output.
573: 
574: Data governance WP-5066 catalogs legacy HR finance folders still containing payroll accrual true-up spreadsheets. Those folders are evidentiary only; extractor output must come from canonical structured sections.
575: 
576: SOX testing team WP-1031 linked retroactive status conflict on payroll accrual true-up to a manual override logged at 02:14 local time between two automated correction imports.
577: 
578: Fixed-assets specialist K. Morales argued that payroll accrual true-up capitalization memos should not alter ledger status; investigators agreed while noting those memos still inform exception coding narratives.
579: 
580: Audit technologist S. Patel replayed FY24 mailbox snapshots and showed how payroll accrual true-up threads arrived out of order relative to correction notices, surfacing mailbox ingestion lag on four high-balance rows.
581: 
582: Committee packet #801 chronicles how payroll accrual true-up escalated after J. Huang observed ledger slice confusion between two correction batches. Cross-checks against amendment minutes were required before accepting any owner change.
583: 
584: Grant compliance WP-9154 tied payroll accrual true-up attestation gaps to mailbox ingestion lag visible only when hold flags used corrected rather than pre-correction ledger dates.
585: 
586: Peer review #528 of HR finance sampling found 17 mislinked emails on payroll accrual true-up. None of the mislinked messages originated from compliance addresses, supporting Brief 02 sender restrictions.
